    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations by adapting to students’ confidence levels—flaging tricky steps with analogies or interactive examples. For example, a chatbot could simulate solving equations step-by-step while asking ‘What if we adjust b?’ to reinforce understanding. Gamification (e.g., quizzes) and real-world math applications (like coding prompts) could also bridge gaps between theory and practice."
